{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"**Slice 1 is not accepted.** The four saved default packages passed their store checks, and both forged packages failed for the exact recorded reasons. The blocker is certification. I gave the two August checks the saved September 20 packages instead. Both passed, and the acceptance script’s final decision reported zero failures. [Saved refusal results:44597](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23f/results.json:44597) · [release_check.py:266](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:266)\n\n### Round 75e findings\n\n| Finding | Status in 75f |\n|---|---|\n| A genuine quote copied to the wrong question passed Test 2 | **The reported case is closed.** The test now requires the exact question, evidence ID, field and text for both genuine occurrences. Its scan of other questions’ evidence still covers only summaries and quotes. The production checker separately compares every evidence and source field with the store. [test_release.py:223](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:223) · [release.py:317](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:317) |\n| Tests 11 and 21 accepted an incomplete report | **Closed.** Both compare the complete counts, both unresolved questions and their reasons, and exactly 3,313 bytes against fixed fixture values. [test_release.py:41](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:41) · [test_release.py:458](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:458) · [test_release.py:643](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:643) |\n| A changed marker or an empty June `old-2` result passed | **Both reported examples are closed.** The marker is fixed independently. Every default report must match its expected day, classes and evidence count. The historical package dates still have the gap described below. [release_check.py:23](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:23) · [release_check.py:255](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:255) · [release_check.py:264](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:264) |\n| A placeholder could stand in for the forecast, and Tests 8 and 10 accepted loose reasons | **The placeholder and both named refusal cases are closed.** I checked that both saved forgeries contain the full 315-character forecast from judgement 1580. The script itself verifies only a prefix. Tests 8 and 10 now require their exact messages. [release_check.py:191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:191) · [release_check.py:201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:201) · [test_release.py:294](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:294) · [test_release.py:343](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:343) · [test_release.py:364](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:364) |\n\n### Two certification gaps\n\n1. **A September package can pass as an August release.** For `old-3`, the substitution increased the evidence count from 3,239 to 6,659. For `old-1`, it increased from 5,673 to 8,251. The script looks up the judgement on the requested August day, but never compares that day with the returned package’s `as_of`. Both September answers were still “Yes,” so every historical assertion passed. The saved August packages are correctly dated. The decisive check is to compare the returned package date with the requested day. [release_check.py:206](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:206) · [release_check.py:266](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:266) · [August 25 report:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23f/old-3/package-2026-08-25.report.json:11) · [August 28 report:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23f/old-1/package-2026-08-28.report.json:11)\n2. **The package can declare the wrong format or allow-list version and still be certified if a production constant drifts.** Revision 11 fixes both identifiers at `/1`. In two separate in-memory checks, I changed one constant and its corresponding package identifier to `/2`. Each passed all 91,055 `old-1` comparisons at the original byte size. The writer and checker share those constants, and the acceptance script checks neither identifier independently. A literal comparison of both identifiers on the delivered package closes this gap. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:115) · [release.py:157](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:157) · [release.py:296](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:296) · [release_check.py:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:254)\n\n**Optional under §5.** The blanket claim about *every* assertion is still too broad. The test helper takes its expected day from the export. Some occupied-path tests check only `FileExistsError` or exit status. These and the narrower quote scan do not independently let a wrong package through. The production builder already passes its separately resolved day into the staged check. I would stop after the two demonstrated certification gaps and verify them against the saved packages. All review work was read-only. [test_release.py:172](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:172) · [test_release.py:321](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:321) · [test_release.py:486](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:486) · [test_release.py:579](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:579) · [release_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:61)"}}
